+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""session_runner — carries out model S-012's plan entries in five separate steps (model S-014).
+
+Usage:
+  session_runner.py pack --entry FILE --source DIR --now RFC3339 --control FILE
+                         [--pack DIR] [--config DIR] [--request-month YYYY-MM]
+                         [--builder-control FILE --builder-hash HEX]
+  session_runner.py run --pack DIR --control FILE --control-hash HEX --out DIR [--claude PATH]
+  session_runner.py collect --pack DIR --control FILE --control-hash HEX --out DIR
+  session_runner.py checks --source DIR --changes DIR --control FILE --control-hash HEX
+                           --builder-control FILE --builder-hash HEX --work DIR --out DIR
+  session_runner.py record --dest DIR --outcomes FILE --step CONTROL HASH DIR [--step ...]
+
+Each step reads only the paths on its command line (AC1).
+
+  pack     A plan entry (one JSON object from status/plan.json: item, route, action,
+           role, stage, spec, gate), the source tree, and the configuration (--config,
+           default the source tree: governance/PACKS.toml, RUNNER.toml, BRIEFS.toml,
+           ROUTING.toml, SURFACES.md and .claude/agents/) -> the pack folder and,
+           outside it, the sealed control file (AC2-AC5). Prints the control file's
+           sha256, which every later step takes as a separate argument and checks.
+           A `run-checks` entry gets a control file only (no --pack), naming the
+           builder's control file by its hash (--builder-control, --builder-hash).
+           An entry for an unknown role gets a control file marked refused (exit 1),
+           which `record` reports as `error` (J1). --request-month names the month of
+           the item's request, the first dispatch-log month Triage receives; without
+           it Triage receives every month file up to --now's month.
+  run      Starts the pinned command line in the pack with the role's exact tool
+           set and a minimal environment (AC6, AC7); writes answer.txt, stderr.txt
+           and result.json to --out (outside the pack). The only step that starts a
+           program other than the runner, and that program is the command line.
+  collect  For a builder-class role, compares the finished pack with the control
+           file's manifest and keeps only safe changes inside the lane (AC8):
+           --out/changes.json, --out/files/<path>, --out/discards.txt. A read-only
+           role gets an empty change set.
+  checks   Copies the source tree without .git, the holdouts and credential files,
+           applies the change set, restores the locked checks and the builder's
+           test-helper files, and runs governance/checks/check_all.sh there with no
+           secrets (AC9): --out/check.log, --out/result.json, --out/discards.txt.
+           The only step that runs project code.
+  record   For each --step (a control file, its hash, and the folder `run` or
+           `checks` wrote, or `-` for a refused entry), writes the record under
+           --dest byte for byte and appends one line to --outcomes with exactly the
+           keys model S-012 reads (AC10).
+
+Exit 0 = done, 1 = the entry was refused (pack), 2 = usage error or refusal (a control
+file that does not match its hash, a tampered pack, a path outside the destination).
